top and want to download your first QR-Based Library System presentation as a PowerPoint (.pptx) file, you'll need to open your presentation in the editor first. Here’s how you can do it:</p><div class="xlh3980 xvmahel x1ghz6dp x1wtentn x1n2zxk4 x1sk33t8 x7gbg69 xli2zx2 x1958duc x12oo3zp x8d2oow x1mzt3pk x1vvkbs x1yc453h x1hx0egp xce744n LbzErQ"><ol class="_8k16_w" start="1"><li>From your Canva Home page, find your QR-Based Library System presentation.</li><li>Hover over its thumbnail and select it to open the presentation in the editor.</li><li>In the editor, go to the top menu and select <b>Share</b>.</li><li>Select <b>Download</b>.</li><li>From the File type dropdown, choose <b>PPTX</b>.</li><li>If your presentation has multiple pages, select the pages you want to download or leave it set to all pages.</li><li>Select <b>Download</b>.</li></ol></div><p class="xlh3980 xvmahel x1ghz6dp x1wtentn x1n2zxk4 x1sk33t8 x7gbg69 xli2zx2 x1958duc x12oo3zp x8d2oow x1mzt3pk x1vvkbs x1yc453h x1hx0egp xce744n LbzErQ">Your file will be compatible with PowerPoint 2024. Let me know if you need help with anything else!</p></div></div></div></div></div><div role="group" aria-label="Provide feedback" class="x1ghz6dp xng3xce xc342km xe8uvvx x9f619 x1a2a7pz xzfypkh xce744n x17m7gxz x7yrpt8 x1fozly0 PBaNoA" style="--x-borderRadius: var(--x14jesot); --x-padding: 4px;"><div class="x78zum5 xdt5ytf xeuugli"><div class="x1ghz6dp x1717udv xe8uvvx x78zum5 x1q0g3np x1a02dak xlqzeqv x1eywl5b x1r8uycs xo0oibl" style="--x-columnGap: 8px; --x-rowGap: 8px; --x-alignItems: center;"><div class="x1q0g3np xeuugli x1lliihq"><div class="xjp7ctv"><button class="x1lfrg59 xng3xce xc342km x6s0dn4 x14fvlzd x9f619 x1ypdohk x3nfvp2 xxymvpz x193iq5w x1oi6v9h x1u9bxl0 xlh3980 xvmahel x1ghz6dp x1wtentn x1n2zxk4 x1sk33t8 x7gbg69 xli2zx2 x1egkzza x12oo3zp x8d2oow x1mzt3pk x1vvkbs xcoeub6 xi9wb9w xxby36a x1j731v2 x1wfmkp7 xl56j7k xt970qd xk3hrty x1ajfcz2 xaaagfd xw1cjtq x4azft0 x1bsd2ls xvb79w2 x1riweet xdhdacu x17ewvzc